    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0493" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg409"/>

                <head>No. 208.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hardinge to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 10, 1886</date>.
                        [Received August 11.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of yesterday, drawing the attention of Her Majesty’s Government to
                    the alleged unwarrantable and unfriendly treatment experienced by the American
                    fishing schooner Battler, on the 3d instant, upon the occasion of her being
                    driven by stress of weather to find shelter in the harbor of Shelburne, Nova
                    Scotia.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>CHARLES HARDINGE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
